# Keep line endings stable across machines (developed on Windows).
* text=auto eol=lf

# BINARY, AND THE LIST HAS TO BE COMPLETE. `* text=auto` makes git guess, and a guess of
# "text" on an image means CRLF normalisation runs through the bytes. Only *.png was
# listed, so the four .jfif source photographs were tracked as text and one careless
# normalisation pass would have corrupted them silently - checked on 2026-08-17 and they
# survived, but only because they were restored before the commit.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.jfif binary
*.webp binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
